course: dictionary
lesson: 10082
title: One small word, many jobs: then
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Then» is a tiny word with lots of jobs. Most often it means next, or after that. «The octopus pretends to be a lionfish and then a sea snake.» First one trick, then the next. Read the words before and after «then» to find out which job it is doing.
explain: Sometimes «then» points back in time. «I was little then» means at that time. «Since then» and «by then» work the same way. Ask yourself: is this about the order of things, or about a time?
explain: «Then» can also mean so, or in that case. «If it rains, then we stay in.» The rain is the reason, and staying in is what follows. Try swapping in «in that case». If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Careful: «than» is a different word. You use «than» to compare, as in «bigger than». Writing «then» when you mean «than» is a common typing mistake, so check it before you finish.
fact: «Then» usually means next, or after that: «and then», «just then», «but then».
fact: «Then» can mean at that time, as in «Then Mum saw the glow under her door.»
fact: «Then» can mean so or in that case, as in «If it rains, then we stay in».
fact: At the end of a question, «then» means so: «What then?» Casual talk also says «Right then, let's go».
fact: Formal writing uses words like «subsequently», «thereafter» and «at that time» instead of «then».
exercise: «Toad thinks a long time and then says sadly, "You have conquered, my friends."» What does then mean here? | So, in that case | Pretty and bright | *Next, after that | Before that, at the very start
exercise: «If it rains, then we stay in.» What does then mean in this sentence? | At that time in the past | Next, after that | Pretty and bright | *So, in that case
exercise: Pick the right word: «Then Mum saw the glow under her door.» Which phrase could replace then? | Than | Yesterday | *At that time | Never
test: «Imagine being so slow that green algae grow in your hair, then remember that the same sloth can swim across a river.» What does then mean? | At that time | So, in that case | *Next, after that | Than, as in bigger than
test: Pick the right word: «I was little ___.» (meaning at that time) | *then | ten | than | the
exam: Which everyday word could replace «thereafter» in «The bell rang, and thereafter the class went home»? | there | never | *then | than
